# Keep Parc's code out of Chromium

Use a Chromium extension point first, then Parc-owned code under `Engine/Parc*`.
Any new or larger patch, hook, Chromium header edit or Chromium BUILD edit is a
last resort. Try the alternatives against the real code and write down why
each fails for behaviour, speed, protected media, security fixes, upgrades and
rebuilds. Then tell the user plainly and wait for their approval of that change.
No exception for small, temporary, test-only or release-blocking changes.
See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#chromium-boundary).
